"""RetailPulse data generator.

Standard library only, so it runs in a Databricks notebook or on your laptop.

Notebook use (file sits next to your notebook in the Git folder):

    import retailpulse_generator as g
    g.generate(root="/Volumes/retailpulse/raw/landing", days=120)      # history
    g.generate(root="/Volumes/retailpulse/raw/landing", live=True)     # one new batch "now"
    g.generate(root="/Volumes/retailpulse/raw/landing", live=True, drift=True)  # adds new columns

Command line use:

    python retailpulse_generator.py --root ./landing --days 120
    python retailpulse_generator.py --root ./landing --live

Output folders under root: orders, customers, products, clicks, tickets, docs.
The data contains deliberate flaws (duplicates, nulls, negative amounts, late events,
inconsistent casing) so the cleaning and data quality phases have real work to do.
"""
